# Firmware binaries are NOT committed. They are fetched from GitHub Releases by
# scripts\05_check_repo.ps1 (bench) and scripts\06_fetch_plant_firmware.ps1
# (plant), each verified against the .sha256 that CI generated beside it.
#
# Two reasons, and the second is the important one:
#   1. They are ~1 MB each and would bloat every clone forever.
#   2. A binary committed here would drift from the release it claims to be.
#      Fetching means the checksum is always the one CI produced for that exact
#      image, and the plant firmware only lands on a laptop when somebody
#      deliberately asks for it.
#
# NO binary is committed here at all, including boot_app0.bin. That file is
# framework-supplied and identical across releases -- verified byte-identical
# between the v1.0.0 build set and the v1.1.0 release asset -- so
# 06_fetch_plant_firmware.ps1 pulls it from the release alongside the app
# image. This keeps the tree consistent with the repo's root .gitignore, which
# ignores *.bin globally and admits exceptions only via a deliberate
# `git add -f`.
artifacts/bench/*.bin
artifacts/bench/*.sha256
artifacts/bench/VERSION.txt
artifacts/plant-v1.0.2/*.bin
artifacts/plant-v1.0.2/*.sha256

# Whatever a visit captures is evidence from that visit, not repo content.
evidence/*
!evidence/.gitkeep
!.gitkeep
